WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:02:02.225 --> 00:02:04.266
How could he have baptized them?


00:02:04.466 --> 00:02:07.585
It's just an ordinary river.


00:02:11.626 --> 00:02:13.946
Only Jews let themselves be baptized


00:02:14.186 --> 00:02:16.827
in an ordinary, dirty and stinky river.


00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:27.835
<i>Welcome to Sobibor!</i>


00:03:30.475 --> 00:03:34.715
<i>Welcome to your new lives!</i>


00:03:36.795 --> 00:03:39.755
<i>This is your home now.</i>


00:03:49.877 --> 00:03:52.877
<i>Welcome to Sobibor!</i>


00:03:55.678 --> 00:03:59.638
<i>Welcome to your new lives!</i>


00:04:02.239 --> 00:04:05.158
<i>This is your home now.</i>


00:04:49.484 --> 00:04:52.444
I wonder for how long
they're going to separate us.


00:04:54.804 --> 00:04:56.764
What will it be like?


00:04:57.604 --> 00:05:00.925
Three entire days!


00:05:01.965 --> 00:05:04.365
It's all because of their German order.


00:05:04.765 --> 00:05:07.006
They're crazy about order.


00:05:07.606 --> 00:05:09.565
Can we trust Germans?


00:05:10.526 --> 00:05:12.326
You're panicking again!


00:05:12.526 --> 00:05:14.766
What a nervous companion I've got!


00:05:15.006 --> 00:05:17.366
Jacob, we'll work as usual.


00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:19.727
And we are immortal.


00:05:20.966 --> 00:05:22.807
Why is that?


00:05:23.047 --> 00:05:25.088
Because we are jewelers.


00:05:25.328 --> 00:05:28.047
And gold is stronger than death.


00:05:36.249 --> 00:05:38.648
You will get your suitcases later.


00:05:39.849 --> 00:05:41.649
Everything will be safe.


00:05:42.329 --> 00:05:44.249
Don't worry.


00:05:44.489 --> 00:05:46.009
I won't.


00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:47.530
Thank you.


00:06:31.654 --> 00:06:34.055
<i>Welcome to the Sobibor camp.</i>


00:06:36.816 --> 00:06:40.456
Here you'll be able to work diligently
and live in dignity


00:06:40.616 --> 00:06:43.696
until your relocation
to lands liberated by the Reich.


00:06:52.897 --> 00:06:54.138
Don't worry.


00:06:54.378 --> 00:06:56.457
The separation of men and women
is temporary.


00:07:00.737 --> 00:07:04.338
Due to health and safety concerns,
you need to take a shower.


00:07:04.578 --> 00:07:07.458
This is necessary to avoid
a typhus epidemic.


00:07:10.299 --> 00:07:13.939
It's a bit boring,
but first things first.


00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:19.620
After, you'll all see each other again.


00:07:23.381 --> 00:07:26.501
Keep your vouchers, so that you can
easily find your luggage


00:07:26.701 --> 00:07:28.501
and get settled in your houses.


00:07:28.741 --> 00:07:31.061
You should take up any work.


00:07:31.301 --> 00:07:32.781
Why?


00:07:33.021 --> 00:07:34.782
So that you stay alive.


00:07:37.862 --> 00:07:39.622
Are there any craftsmen here?


00:07:39.902 --> 00:07:42.342
Shoemakers, carpenters,


00:07:42.582 --> 00:07:44.543
blacksmiths, saddlemakers?


00:07:44.743 --> 00:07:47.943
Seamstresses, dressmakers?


00:07:48.703 --> 00:07:50.343
Jewelers?


00:07:50.583 --> 00:07:51.824
I'm a jeweler!


00:07:52.024 --> 00:07:53.663
Him as well, he's my partner.


00:07:53.943 --> 00:07:55.104
Jewelers?


00:07:55.784 --> 00:07:57.344
I am a jeweler.


00:07:57.544 --> 00:07:59.185
Look at this ring.


00:07:59.465 --> 00:08:00.864
I've made it.


00:08:01.104 --> 00:08:03.505
My wife's engagement ring.


00:08:03.745 --> 00:08:05.945
Great.
We'll find use for jewelers.


00:08:11.066 --> 00:08:13.586
What'd I tell you?
Stick with me, Jacob!


00:08:18.426 --> 00:08:19.666
Seamstresses,


00:08:20.587 --> 00:08:22.147
dressmakers!


00:08:44.909 --> 00:08:47.469
Do not deviate from the order.


00:08:47.709 --> 00:08:50.550
You are to undress completely.


00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:52.950
The women will shower first.


00:09:12.552 --> 00:09:15.153
I'll go with you.
Mom, Dad, go without us.


00:09:15.393 --> 00:09:17.913
I want to stay with Shlomo.


00:09:21.634 --> 00:09:24.634
Rivka, Mom and Dad will be angry.


00:09:24.914 --> 00:09:28.155
I'll make pretty earrings for you
and bring them to you tomorrow.


00:09:28.354 --> 00:09:30.794
Small ones, with blue stones.


00:09:31.234 --> 00:09:34.274
I don't want blue stones,
I want red ones!


00:09:35.475 --> 00:09:36.875
Rivka,


00:09:38.075 --> 00:09:40.555
your brother needs to get ready.


00:09:40.795 --> 00:09:42.115
It won't take long.


00:09:42.996 --> 00:09:44.796
He was entrusted with a job.


00:09:49.436 --> 00:09:51.237
It's very important.


00:09:51.477 --> 00:09:54.597
Don't scratch your pimple,
it'll leave a mark!


00:09:55.117 --> 00:09:57.318
I'll put some turpentine on it tomorrow.


00:09:58.997 --> 00:10:00.157
Mom!


00:10:02.998 --> 00:10:04.878
See you in the morning, son.


00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.520
Finally we can have a shower!


00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:25.200
Yes, two days' travel without a shower
is terrible!


00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:30.201
Hurry up and take them away!


00:10:31.041 --> 00:10:33.161
Move along, move along!


00:10:34.121 --> 00:10:36.282
Keep the child by your side.


00:10:38.802 --> 00:10:40.482
God, how much longer?


00:10:40.722 --> 00:10:42.242
You're there already.


00:10:55.724 --> 00:10:57.563
Stop.
Go on!


00:13:16.139 --> 00:13:17.740
- Wagner!
- What?


00:13:18.539 --> 00:13:20.739
What do you think?


00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:23.420
Does it get him going,
or does nothing work for him anymore?


00:14:36.948 --> 00:14:39.709
They got here from Minsk camp -


00:14:40.429 --> 00:14:42.948
they tried to escape but it didn't work.


00:14:43.949 --> 00:14:46.790
I'm surprised they weren't killed.


00:14:47.389 --> 00:14:49.229
Kick the Russian out of here!


00:15:01.951 --> 00:15:04.351
Why are you telling us that?


00:15:05.671 --> 00:15:07.591
I'm just introducing myself.


00:15:07.831 --> 00:15:10.272
We're peaceful people, artisans.


00:15:10.512 --> 00:15:13.552
We're alive only because we follow
the rules.


00:15:13.792 --> 00:15:15.112
You're a provocateur.


00:15:15.352 --> 00:15:17.192
And if we report you?


00:15:17.472 --> 00:15:20.473
Why weren't you shot in Minsk?


00:15:21.113 --> 00:15:23.753
My brothers think you're not a Jew.


00:15:23.993 --> 00:15:25.593
Enough.


00:15:36.274 --> 00:15:38.395
Look.


00:15:41.635 --> 00:15:43.475
I'm circumcised - like you.


00:15:46.435 --> 00:15:48.356
I'm a Jew - like you.


00:16:16.719 --> 00:16:19.960
Some kind of underground they got here.
Quivering and praying.


00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:22.359
Cowards.


00:16:22.559 --> 00:16:24.560
They're like livestock going
to the slaughter.


00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:26.080
Damn kikes!


00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:30.000
Sasha, let's leave without them.
I'll gnaw through this wire myself.


00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:33.520
- They'll shoot you from a watchtower.
- Don't jinx it!


00:16:48.322 --> 00:16:50.963
So, Sasha, what is your decision?


00:16:53.883 --> 00:16:56.524
We've only been here for two days
and they've been here for a long time.


00:16:56.764 --> 00:16:58.523
They know the camp
and the surroundings.


00:16:58.763 --> 00:17:00.724
It's okay.
We'll win them over.


00:17:02.364 --> 00:17:03.804
Let's go.


00:17:44.568 --> 00:17:46.329
Mom only saw things like this
in shop windows.


00:17:46.529 --> 00:17:47.889
Can you imagine?


00:17:48.129 --> 00:17:49.970
We didn't even dare to get close


00:17:50.249 --> 00:17:52.769
out of fear that we could've broken something.


00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:55.410
But I promised to myself
that I'd give my mom


00:17:55.650 --> 00:17:57.650
all the treasures of the world!


00:17:57.890 --> 00:17:59.930
So, did you?


00:18:00.691 --> 00:18:02.610
No, I didn't.


00:18:04.491 --> 00:18:07.532
I could only look at them and admire.


00:18:08.451 --> 00:18:10.131
But now I'll make up for it!


00:18:14.532 --> 00:18:16.572
The Jews have plenty of those!


00:18:19.733 --> 00:18:21.172
But, as they say,


00:18:22.893 --> 00:18:25.813
you can't take anything
to your grave, sadly.


00:18:26.853 --> 00:18:29.014
It doesn't belong to Jews anymore,


00:18:29.214 --> 00:18:32.013
it belongs to the German Reich.


00:18:33.134 --> 00:18:34.894
Don't spoil it, Wagner.


00:18:38.254 --> 00:18:40.575
It would fit my aristocratic hands well.


00:18:41.975 --> 00:18:44.455
Aristocratic?
How?


00:18:44.695 --> 00:18:48.056
You've been working on a construction site
with my brother.


00:19:04.497 --> 00:19:06.018
Wolff, this is for you!


00:19:06.258 --> 00:19:08.378
This would be perfect for you!


00:19:08.578 --> 00:19:10.658
Look, Beckmann!


00:19:11.018 --> 00:19:13.338
You look great!


00:19:13.778 --> 00:19:15.499
A Pretty Jew!


00:19:15.699 --> 00:19:17.659
Welcome to the third camp.


00:19:17.899 --> 00:19:19.979
Into the showers, please,
for disinfection.


00:20:12.384 --> 00:20:14.345
<i>I am a jeweler.</i>


00:20:14.585 --> 00:20:16.145
<i>Look at this ring.</i>


00:20:16.386 --> 00:20:17.826
<i>I made it.</i>


00:20:18.065 --> 00:20:20.066
<i>My wife's engagement ring.</i>


00:20:22.586 --> 00:20:23.547
Good!


00:20:23.787 --> 00:20:26.506
I'll have an exhibition after the war.


00:20:26.706 --> 00:20:28.587
You will all die of jealousy.


00:21:22.313 --> 00:21:24.232
You're not allowed to go out.


00:21:24.433 --> 00:21:26.673
Not after lights-out.


00:21:28.274 --> 00:21:31.153
I didn't go out.
You imagined it.


00:21:33.874 --> 00:21:36.394
I saw you leaving the barrack, Sasha.


00:21:36.634 --> 00:21:38.635
Are you up to something again?


00:21:40.914 --> 00:21:42.475
No.


00:21:44.475 --> 00:21:46.276
Why do you...


00:21:46.515 --> 00:21:48.755
Why do you tempt fate?


00:21:59.836 --> 00:22:01.677
Try and forget about Minsk.


00:22:09.238 --> 00:22:10.998
It wasn't your fault.


00:22:11.238 --> 00:22:12.798
You're alive.


00:22:17.999 --> 00:22:19.759
Don't you want to live?


00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:26.920
No, Luka.


00:22:29.040 --> 00:22:30.960
Not like this.


00:22:33.161 --> 00:22:35.200
Nobody wants to live this way.


00:22:35.440 --> 00:22:37.081
Nobody.


00:22:37.601 --> 00:22:39.562
But we need to endure it.


00:22:40.241 --> 00:22:42.441
Endure and have faith.


00:23:53.329 --> 00:23:55.890
It's impossible to escape from the camp.


00:23:56.769 --> 00:24:00.610
You've been warned, dear Jews.


00:24:01.210 --> 00:24:04.650
Everyone should know:
escapees will die


00:24:04.890 --> 00:24:07.531
and innocent people will pay
with their lives for them.


00:24:07.731 --> 00:24:12.051
That's how it was before,
and that's how it'll always be.


00:24:12.612 --> 00:24:14.571
So, watch each other carefully.


00:24:14.771 --> 00:24:18.492
And report any suspicious activity
to your kapos, gentlemen!


00:24:18.732 --> 00:24:19.893
Jews!


00:24:20.132 --> 00:24:22.852
And now, we'll shoot every
tenth one of you.


00:24:23.092 --> 00:24:25.093
Cruel, but just.


00:24:25.733 --> 00:24:27.373
On your knees!


00:24:39.294 --> 00:24:42.575
One, two, three, four, five,


00:24:42.815 --> 00:24:46.055
six, seven, eight, nine, ten.


00:24:46.255 --> 00:24:49.536
One, two, three, four, five,


00:24:49.775 --> 00:24:53.136
six, seven, eight, nine, ten.


00:24:53.376 --> 00:24:56.336
One, two, three, four, five,


00:24:56.816 --> 00:24:59.657
six, seven, eight, nine, ten.


00:24:59.897 --> 00:25:02.777
Hey, Gustav, don't hurry!
You're breaking the rhythm.


00:25:04.217 --> 00:25:07.337
One, two, three, four, five,


00:25:07.537 --> 00:25:10.058
six, seven, eight, nine, ten.


00:25:10.578 --> 00:25:13.058
One, two, three, four, five,


00:25:13.297 --> 00:25:15.978
six, seven, eight, nine, ten.


00:25:16.218 --> 00:25:18.499
One, two, three, four, five,


00:25:18.739 --> 00:25:21.979
six, seven, eight, nine...


00:26:30.866 --> 00:26:32.587
What are you doing, Jews?


00:26:42.027 --> 00:26:44.268
You deserve your fate!


00:26:44.508 --> 00:26:45.948
Go to sleep.


00:26:54.229 --> 00:26:58.390
The ashes of your relatives
fly into your faces.


00:27:00.509 --> 00:27:02.430
And you're just swallowing it?


00:27:04.551 --> 00:27:06.150
Damn you!


00:27:09.671 --> 00:27:12.431
Why are you lying?
My sister is alive.


00:27:13.071 --> 00:27:16.272
I've made earrings
with red stones for her.


00:27:17.152 --> 00:27:19.152
My dear dad is alive.


00:27:20.032 --> 00:27:22.152
The Germans promised me!


00:27:22.593 --> 00:27:24.352
And Germans keep their word.


00:27:29.793 --> 00:27:31.433
Damn you...


00:27:32.233 --> 00:27:34.314
Damn you all!


00:27:34.754 --> 00:27:36.954
Damn you all!


00:27:37.194 --> 00:27:39.234
Go to sleep, son of a bitch!


00:27:39.474 --> 00:27:43.314
Damn you all!
Damn you all!


00:28:38.001 --> 00:28:40.520
<i>I'll go with you.
Mom, Dad, go without us.</i>


00:28:40.760 --> 00:28:43.561
<i>I want to stay with Shlomo.</i>


00:28:46.321 --> 00:28:49.162
<i>Rivka, Mom and Dad will be angry.</i>


00:28:49.402 --> 00:28:52.322
<i>I'll make pretty earrings for you
and bring them to you tomorrow.</i>


00:28:52.522 --> 00:28:54.362
<i>Small ones, with blue stones.</i>


00:28:55.683 --> 00:28:58.882
<i>I don't want blue stones,
I want red ones!</i>


00:30:42.654 --> 00:30:46.174
Yes, we have a committee.
You guessed correctly.


00:30:50.215 --> 00:30:53.135
We need a commander
with military experience.


00:30:55.376 --> 00:30:57.816
We had this Dutch man, Joseph Jacobs,


00:30:58.016 --> 00:31:00.336
a Navy officer, a brave guy.


00:31:02.056 --> 00:31:04.296
He led our preparations


00:31:05.017 --> 00:31:08.497
but kapo Berliner found out about it
and reported him.


00:31:09.577 --> 00:31:11.978
They've been torturing the Dutchman
for two days


00:31:12.218 --> 00:31:14.337
but he didn't give us away.


00:31:16.258 --> 00:31:19.179
But the Germans shot 76 Jews anyway.


00:31:19.418 --> 00:31:21.418
And my Jews have lost their heart.


00:31:25.019 --> 00:31:28.419
How many receipts did your committee
give to the people at the station?


00:31:28.659 --> 00:31:31.699
You promised them that it would be fine,
didn't you?


00:31:35.460 --> 00:31:37.180
We're trying to survive


00:31:37.420 --> 00:31:38.860
to get our revenge.


00:31:41.541 --> 00:31:43.580
You're just trying to survive.


00:32:16.345 --> 00:32:18.105
One Reich, one Fuhrer!


00:33:00.509 --> 00:33:02.469
Found anything interesting?


00:33:03.630 --> 00:33:06.910
I haven't seen the kind of cuff links
that you want yet.


00:33:09.670 --> 00:33:12.150
You aren't looking well enough!


00:33:13.150 --> 00:33:15.271
You've been lazy!


00:33:16.511 --> 00:33:18.871
You are very lazy!


00:33:24.552 --> 00:33:27.392
Do you think I like beating you?


00:33:29.353 --> 00:33:31.353
This is all I've found.


00:33:32.193 --> 00:33:34.473
These are the things from the Paris train.


00:33:42.714 --> 00:33:43.914
Oh, wow.


00:33:45.434 --> 00:33:47.354
Must be from a banker!


00:33:48.594 --> 00:33:51.155
Wagner will piss himself with jealousy.


00:33:52.355 --> 00:33:54.435
Does Wagner have something like this?


00:33:54.675 --> 00:33:57.316
I've never seen anything like this.


00:33:58.676 --> 00:34:00.956
Expensive leather.
From the Chanel house.


00:34:03.557 --> 00:34:04.956
What a smell!


00:34:06.276 --> 00:34:10.757
Have you ever heard of leather
smelling like flowers?


00:34:10.997 --> 00:34:12.277
It smells lovely.


00:34:15.318 --> 00:34:19.478
Well, I should reward you
for your good work.


00:34:20.838 --> 00:34:21.879
C0gnac!


00:34:22.718 --> 00:34:26.399
Everything is French today,
it's not to be sneezed at!


00:34:30.639 --> 00:34:31.879
Drink it.


00:34:33.280 --> 00:34:35.239
I'm a Jew, I can't have Cognac.


00:34:35.479 --> 00:34:36.720
Why?


00:34:37.360 --> 00:34:39.521
Our faith doesn't allow it.


00:34:39.761 --> 00:34:41.440
Do you have faith?


00:34:41.920 --> 00:34:43.521
All of us do.


00:34:46.160 --> 00:34:47.521
Pants off.


00:34:51.122 --> 00:34:53.401
25 lashes.
Count them.


00:34:53.642 --> 00:34:56.282
If you lose count, I'll start again.


00:35:01.923 --> 00:35:03.043
One.


00:35:03.962 --> 00:35:04.843
Two.


00:35:05.043 --> 00:35:07.363
Wrong.
Start over.


00:35:07.603 --> 00:35:08.884
One.


00:35:09.923 --> 00:35:11.283
- Two.
- Louder!


00:35:12.244 --> 00:35:13.484
One!


00:35:14.444 --> 00:35:15.645
<i>Two!</i>


00:35:16.444 --> 00:35:17.644
- Three!
- Louder!


00:35:18.364 --> 00:35:19.765
Four!


00:35:20.005 --> 00:35:21.085
<i>Five!</i>


00:35:21.644 --> 00:35:22.765
Six!


00:35:24.245 --> 00:35:25.645
Seven!


00:35:25.886 --> 00:35:27.406
Eight!


00:35:28.325 --> 00:35:29.966
Nope.
From the beginning!


00:35:30.206 --> 00:35:31.606
One.


00:35:31.846 --> 00:35:33.287
Two.


00:35:33.486 --> 00:35:34.806
Three.


00:35:35.046 --> 00:35:36.326
Four.


00:35:36.527 --> 00:35:37.847
<i>Five!</i>


00:35:38.047 --> 00:35:39.606
<i>Six!</i>


00:35:39.846 --> 00:35:41.367
<i>Seven!</i>


00:36:04.809 --> 00:36:06.490
Stop tormenting yourself.


00:36:09.410 --> 00:36:11.090
You can't live like that.


00:36:28.332 --> 00:36:30.573
They're expecting miracles from me.


00:36:31.973 --> 00:36:33.492
And what can I do?


00:36:35.933 --> 00:36:37.854
I was a fool


00:36:38.413 --> 00:36:40.733
playing a hero and a savior in Minsk.


00:36:41.454 --> 00:36:42.974
People died.


00:36:44.894 --> 00:36:46.334
And I'm alive.


00:36:49.375 --> 00:36:50.814
Enough.


00:36:53.975 --> 00:36:55.055
No more games.


00:37:04.376 --> 00:37:06.177
This nightmare will end.


00:37:09.616 --> 00:37:11.337
Some of us will survive.


00:37:15.497 --> 00:37:16.737
Yes.


00:37:19.458 --> 00:37:20.818
For sure.


00:37:23.178 --> 00:37:24.499
And I pray...


00:37:28.179 --> 00:37:29.939
...that it would be you, Sasha.


00:37:34.980 --> 00:37:36.380
God will save us.


00:37:40.820 --> 00:37:42.981
Just don't get in his way.


00:37:46.901 --> 00:37:48.021
Sasha!


00:37:50.261 --> 00:37:52.221
We just need to endure.


00:37:54.782 --> 00:37:56.502
Endure and have faith.


00:37:57.262 --> 00:37:58.902
<i>One!</i>


00:37:59.863 --> 00:38:01.382
<i>Two!</i>


00:38:02.502 --> 00:38:04.143
<i>Three!</i>


00:38:05.423 --> 00:38:06.863
<i>Four!</i>


00:38:07.943 --> 00:38:09.303
<i>Five!</i>


00:38:10.544 --> 00:38:12.064
<i>Six!</i>


00:38:13.183 --> 00:38:14.824
<i>Seven!</i>


00:38:16.024 --> 00:38:17.504
<i>Eight!</i>


00:38:19.064 --> 00:38:20.664
<i>Nine!</i>


00:38:21.705 --> 00:38:22.665
<i>Ten!</i>


00:38:37.346 --> 00:38:39.587
Do you like it?


00:38:42.187 --> 00:38:43.307
No.


00:39:05.670 --> 00:39:08.190
And what if he gave it to you?


00:39:17.111 --> 00:39:18.991
Put the necklace on her.


00:39:19.791 --> 00:39:21.151
Come on.


00:39:45.474 --> 00:39:47.074
She's so beautiful.


00:39:50.754 --> 00:39:52.075
Don't you think?


00:39:55.515 --> 00:39:57.355
Come on,


00:39:58.276 --> 00:39:59.395
tell her.


00:40:07.116 --> 00:40:08.917
You are very beautiful.


00:40:12.997 --> 00:40:15.157
Now kiss her, Jew.


00:40:16.438 --> 00:40:18.117
Kiss her!
Kiss her!


00:40:19.197 --> 00:40:20.678
Come on, kiss her!


00:40:25.878 --> 00:40:28.159
I'm sorry, I can't protect you.


00:40:28.359 --> 00:40:29.878
Do what he says.


00:40:37.440 --> 00:40:39.280
No, no, no!


00:40:40.400 --> 00:40:42.120
More passion!


00:40:42.360 --> 00:40:43.560
<i>More!</i>


00:40:44.681 --> 00:40:46.440
Kiss her with passion!


00:40:46.640 --> 00:40:47.800
Passion!


00:40:48.841 --> 00:40:50.201
Go on!


00:40:50.441 --> 00:40:51.762
Kiss her!


00:40:51.962 --> 00:40:53.641
Keep going, keep going!


00:40:53.881 --> 00:40:55.882
Keep going!
Keep going!


00:40:57.122 --> 00:40:59.562
More, more, more!


00:41:03.803 --> 00:41:06.283
My first woman was a Jew.


00:41:06.483 --> 00:41:10.683
She loved me and I loved her
more than anything in the world.


00:41:11.323 --> 00:41:13.043
We wanted to get married.


00:41:13.604 --> 00:41:16.243
But my father was an anti-Semite


00:41:17.004 --> 00:41:18.404
and he forbade it.


00:41:18.644 --> 00:41:20.004
And I obeyed.


00:41:20.244 --> 00:41:22.044
And she left for America.


00:41:22.244 --> 00:41:24.005
And what am I doing now?


00:41:24.605 --> 00:41:26.005
Killing Jews!


00:41:27.245 --> 00:41:29.045
And whose fault is this?


00:41:29.285 --> 00:41:30.525
Tell me!


00:41:30.725 --> 00:41:32.606
Is it her fault because she left me?


00:41:32.846 --> 00:41:34.245
Or mine only?


00:41:35.086 --> 00:41:36.726
Whose fault is this?


00:41:37.806 --> 00:41:39.886
It's my father's fault.


00:41:40.246 --> 00:41:41.606
It's his fault.


00:41:42.727 --> 00:41:44.247
His fault!


00:41:44.487 --> 00:41:46.807
My father's fault!
My father's!


00:41:47.047 --> 00:41:48.207
My father's!


00:41:48.447 --> 00:41:49.368
My...


00:42:01.049 --> 00:42:03.809
Why is this Jew still alive?


00:43:26.298 --> 00:43:28.258
Hey, you.
Come here!


00:43:51.341 --> 00:43:54.422
I'll give you five minutes
to cut this stump up.


00:43:56.381 --> 00:43:57.781
If you can't do it,


00:43:57.982 --> 00:44:00.422
we'll shoot every tenth person here.


00:44:00.622 --> 00:44:01.942
Understood?


00:44:03.022 --> 00:44:04.582
Five minutes.


00:44:05.223 --> 00:44:06.943
Come on, let's go!


00:45:09.109 --> 00:45:10.590
Hurry up!


00:45:12.110 --> 00:45:13.750
<i>Sasha!</i>


00:45:13.990 --> 00:45:15.870
<i>We just need to endure.</i>


00:45:17.831 --> 00:45:19.550
<i>Endure and have faith.</i>


00:45:41.793 --> 00:45:43.393
Four and a half minutes.


00:45:44.913 --> 00:45:46.034
Good.


00:45:47.474 --> 00:45:48.954
Would you like an apple?


00:45:49.194 --> 00:45:50.394
Thank you,


00:45:50.634 --> 00:45:51.994
but I'm full.


00:45:55.874 --> 00:45:57.355
Take it.


00:45:57.595 --> 00:46:00.315
The food I'm getting here


00:46:01.195 --> 00:46:02.795
is enough for me.


00:46:06.755 --> 00:46:08.436
That's not all.


00:46:26.078 --> 00:46:27.478
Don't be afraid.


00:46:27.718 --> 00:46:29.078
Don't be afraid.


00:46:31.638 --> 00:46:33.359
Would you like some sugar?


00:46:54.721 --> 00:46:56.481
What's your name?


00:46:59.561 --> 00:47:00.842
Keeping silent?


00:47:02.362 --> 00:47:04.203
I'll call you Silent then.


00:47:05.842 --> 00:47:07.122
<i>Silent!</i>


00:47:10.163 --> 00:47:11.563
Okay?


00:47:26.525 --> 00:47:27.685
<i>Silent!</i>


00:47:36.205 --> 00:47:37.926
How long have you been here?


00:47:38.126 --> 00:47:39.526
Almost a year.


00:47:40.646 --> 00:47:42.526
Why are you still alive then?


00:47:43.126 --> 00:47:44.727
Don't be like that, Sasha.


00:47:45.207 --> 00:47:47.087
I'm a good worker


00:47:47.327 --> 00:47:49.687
and everybody needs good workers.


00:48:09.929 --> 00:48:13.930
I was a market director in Gliwice
before the occupation.


00:48:14.930 --> 00:48:16.530
I could do anything,


00:48:16.770 --> 00:48:18.490
I could organize everyone.


00:48:20.531 --> 00:48:22.971
But I won't be able to lead people.


00:48:23.451 --> 00:48:26.171
We need a commander
with military experience.


00:48:31.652 --> 00:48:32.972
Sasha?


00:48:33.451 --> 00:48:35.572
What a typically Jewish approach...


00:48:36.172 --> 00:48:37.693
Yes, Sasha.


00:48:38.653 --> 00:48:40.052
We...


00:48:40.292 --> 00:48:41.773
...need Moses.


00:48:45.773 --> 00:48:47.533
Enough.
Let's sleep.


00:48:48.894 --> 00:48:50.094
Sasha...


00:48:51.373 --> 00:48:53.294
You shouldn't behave like this here.


00:48:54.334 --> 00:48:56.415
You should swallow your pride.


00:48:58.895 --> 00:49:00.455
I'll think about it.


00:49:03.215 --> 00:49:04.415
Sasha!


00:49:38.699 --> 00:49:41.139
They'll report us to Berliner


00:49:41.339 --> 00:49:43.420
if they see us together again.


00:49:45.380 --> 00:49:48.460
They don't want another escape to happen.


00:49:48.861 --> 00:49:51.020
They're afraid of more executions.


00:52:15.837 --> 00:52:17.477
You're drunk again.


00:52:17.676 --> 00:52:19.036
Are you jealous?


00:52:19.277 --> 00:52:21.877
You're 15, but you drink vodka
every evening.


00:52:25.637 --> 00:52:26.998
I'm 100 years old.


00:52:28.038 --> 00:52:30.678
What would your father say?


00:52:30.918 --> 00:52:33.278
He won't say anything anymore.


00:52:33.518 --> 00:52:36.358
Shlomo, you've got hands of gold.


00:52:36.558 --> 00:52:38.799
What are you doing to yourself?


00:52:39.879 --> 00:52:41.439
Hello, kikes.


00:52:45.120 --> 00:52:47.439
Wait...


00:52:50.400 --> 00:52:52.041
Where did you get it?


00:52:52.281 --> 00:52:55.161
Sometimes I find food
among the things I sort


00:52:55.641 --> 00:52:57.721
and manage to hide it.


00:52:58.161 --> 00:53:00.881
Do you want some?
Help yourself, please.


00:53:01.761 --> 00:53:03.482
I won't eat it.


00:53:03.682 --> 00:53:05.161
Leave him.


00:53:06.122 --> 00:53:07.642
Those people are long gone,


00:53:07.882 --> 00:53:09.122
but the food remains.


00:53:09.322 --> 00:53:10.722
Of course, they're gone.


00:53:10.962 --> 00:53:13.203
They've just burnt 100 people
and we're gorging on food in here.


00:53:13.443 --> 00:53:15.563
Why, we're safe here,
wiping Germans' asses!


00:53:15.803 --> 00:53:17.243
Don't be a fool.


00:53:17.483 --> 00:53:19.283
Sasha, everyone is here.


00:53:19.683 --> 00:53:21.564
We need to decide, Sasha.


00:53:25.004 --> 00:53:28.205
Yesterday, Wagner brought some golden teeth


00:53:29.044 --> 00:53:30.925
with pieces of jaw on them


00:53:32.845 --> 00:53:35.845
and asked me to make
a pin for his tie out of them.


00:53:37.765 --> 00:53:39.726
How can I stay sober?


00:55:22.377 --> 00:55:24.937
Work! Work!


00:55:46.299 --> 00:55:47.580
What?


00:55:49.020 --> 00:55:50.299
Easy, easy...


00:55:50.860 --> 00:55:52.020
What?


00:55:52.980 --> 00:55:54.221
Leo, Leo!


00:55:54.461 --> 00:55:56.021
Come here!


00:56:01.822 --> 00:56:03.461
What is he saying?


00:56:17.463 --> 00:56:19.504
Nice shot, isn't it?


00:56:19.743 --> 00:56:21.663
Why so silent?


00:56:23.544 --> 00:56:25.024
What about this one?


00:56:25.983 --> 00:56:29.424
It's a great shot, Mr. Unterscharfuhrer.


00:56:30.905 --> 00:56:33.785
He just can't speak German.


00:56:36.025 --> 00:56:37.545
Forget it.


00:56:38.505 --> 00:56:41.586
<i>Welcome to Sobibor!</i>


00:56:43.825 --> 00:56:47.987
<i>Welcome to your new lives!</i>


00:56:49.746 --> 00:56:52.627
<i>This is your home now.</i>


00:56:56.427 --> 00:56:58.548
He said the train came from Belzec.


00:56:59.068 --> 00:57:02.828
Belzec was liquidated in three days
on the commanders' order.


00:57:04.228 --> 00:57:06.349
And now we're supposed
to utilize the corpses?


00:57:06.589 --> 00:57:07.868
No thanks.


00:57:08.148 --> 00:57:09.429
They've thought it all through.


00:57:19.269 --> 00:57:20.990
Belzec is a camp, like our Sobibor.


00:57:21.230 --> 00:57:23.150
But it's farther east,
closer to the front.


00:57:23.390 --> 00:57:25.030
What was he saying before death?


00:57:25.270 --> 00:57:26.670
Allemen, allemen...


00:57:26.910 --> 00:57:29.151
What does it mean?
What did he want?


00:57:30.191 --> 00:57:31.591
It's Yiddish.


00:57:32.951 --> 00:57:35.112
It means "Avenge us, brothers."


00:57:35.392 --> 00:57:37.391
But how can we avenge them?


00:57:39.792 --> 00:57:40.872
Belzec...


00:57:42.952 --> 00:57:47.033
...was destroyed because Soviet troops
are heading west, to us.


00:57:49.433 --> 00:57:52.674
Maybe we just need to wait
for the Red Army


00:57:53.234 --> 00:57:54.393
and to survive?


00:57:55.073 --> 00:57:56.754
How long should we wait?
A year?


00:57:56.954 --> 00:57:58.234
You won't make it.


00:57:59.915 --> 00:58:02.434
They're going to kill us any day now.


00:58:04.075 --> 00:58:05.195
You, rat!


00:58:05.595 --> 00:58:07.395
I'll kill you, bastard!


00:58:07.635 --> 00:58:08.995
Stop it.


00:58:09.835 --> 00:58:11.116
Stop it.


00:58:24.637 --> 00:58:26.517
Our camp is the next one


00:58:26.757 --> 00:58:28.078
to be liquidated.


00:58:29.278 --> 00:58:31.517
They'll kill everyone - the kapos, too.


00:58:31.798 --> 00:58:35.118
The man on the train
who was shot by Berg,


00:58:35.319 --> 00:58:37.158
was a kapo in Belzec.


00:58:37.438 --> 00:58:39.719
They'll kill all of us together.


00:58:40.759 --> 00:58:42.278
Do you think I'm a sellout?


00:58:42.519 --> 00:58:43.799
I teach physics!


00:58:44.879 --> 00:58:47.200
I've been holding a pointer
in my hands all my life.


00:58:47.439 --> 00:58:48.879
And here I am.


00:58:51.120 --> 00:58:52.440
Have you ever killed people?


00:58:52.680 --> 00:58:54.120
No.


00:58:54.360 --> 00:58:55.760
Can you kill?


00:59:00.040 --> 00:59:01.161
I don't know.


00:59:05.761 --> 00:59:07.722
That's not how a provocateur
would answer.


00:59:12.762 --> 00:59:15.523
He has access to the rooms
where the officers reside.


00:59:16.483 --> 00:59:18.363
There are 12 of them.


00:59:18.563 --> 00:59:20.843
They're the brain of Sobibor.


00:59:21.804 --> 00:59:23.323
If we destroy the brain,


00:59:23.563 --> 00:59:24.763
we'll kill them all.


00:59:26.164 --> 00:59:27.284
How can we do it?


00:59:29.804 --> 00:59:31.124
We'll stab them,


00:59:31.804 --> 00:59:32.885
tear them up,


00:59:33.925 --> 00:59:35.084
strangle them.


00:59:36.765 --> 00:59:38.925
We'll liquidate all the officers,
take their weapons


00:59:39.525 --> 00:59:42.485
and leave through the central gate.


00:59:44.046 --> 00:59:46.485
It'll be easier with weapons...


00:59:46.966 --> 00:59:48.366
Everyone.


00:59:49.766 --> 00:59:51.007
The whole camp.


00:59:53.206 --> 00:59:54.647
How...?


00:59:58.527 --> 01:00:00.247
It's everyone or it's no one.


01:00:02.168 --> 01:00:03.328
Any questions?


01:00:07.048 --> 01:00:08.529
Now leave.


01:00:31.131 --> 01:00:33.492
Tell your people that we need bullets.
They must get them.


01:00:33.691 --> 01:00:35.131
- How?
- I don't know how.


01:00:35.371 --> 01:00:36.811
You're the market director.


01:00:38.532 --> 01:00:40.812
I'll tell the women.
They know how.


01:00:52.853 --> 01:00:54.613
Is it hard to be all alone?


01:00:56.254 --> 01:00:57.333
Hang in there.


01:01:03.015 --> 01:01:04.414
Run.


01:01:07.615 --> 01:01:09.695
Father taught me and Rivka
to forgive people.


01:01:09.935 --> 01:01:11.375
If they are people.


01:01:12.495 --> 01:01:13.976
You are my father now.


01:01:30.097 --> 01:01:31.218
Sasha,


01:01:33.297 --> 01:01:34.658
can we really do it?


01:01:36.738 --> 01:01:38.898
Or will it be the same as in Minsk?


01:01:45.299 --> 01:01:46.499
I don't care


01:01:47.539 --> 01:01:50.499
even if it'll be the same as in Minsk.


01:01:54.580 --> 01:01:56.460
I can't take it anymore.


01:02:15.142 --> 01:02:16.302
Hey!


01:02:16.542 --> 01:02:17.823
Jew!


01:02:49.026 --> 01:02:50.306
Did you steal it?


01:02:53.467 --> 01:02:56.146
Well, I'm in a good mood today.


01:02:56.867 --> 01:02:59.427
Come here, Miss Busty!


01:03:00.187 --> 01:03:01.627
Come here!


01:03:02.107 --> 01:03:04.228
Yes, that's nice.
Oh, yes!


01:03:07.508 --> 01:03:08.708
What is this?


01:03:11.949 --> 01:03:13.468
What is this?


01:03:13.668 --> 01:03:16.309
Where did you get it?
Where?!


01:04:21.156 --> 01:04:22.396
Now what?


01:04:26.357 --> 01:04:29.197
I'll tell the Germans
that Baldy there got sick.


01:04:29.798 --> 01:04:31.917
They won't start looking for him
until tomorrow.


01:04:33.398 --> 01:04:35.038
- Are you sure?
- No.


01:04:38.558 --> 01:04:39.878
So, tomorrow.


01:04:42.958 --> 01:04:44.319
Tomorrow.


01:04:45.879 --> 01:04:49.719
Tomorrow we'll lure all the officers
to the workshop,


01:04:49.959 --> 01:04:52.000
one by one, all 12 of them.


01:04:52.400 --> 01:04:54.719
Three of them will be away on business.


01:04:56.080 --> 01:04:58.240
That leaves us with nine.
Even better.


01:04:59.800 --> 01:05:00.920
Use any excuse.


01:05:01.160 --> 01:05:04.761
Tell them you've got beautiful things
for them - boots, jackets, anything.


01:05:05.001 --> 01:05:08.081
The hardest thing is to lure them in
without arousing suspicion.


01:05:08.321 --> 01:05:09.602
Who can do it?


01:05:12.681 --> 01:05:13.842
<i>I can.</i>


01:05:16.002 --> 01:05:17.282
Thomas.


01:05:17.522 --> 01:05:18.842
You can call me Toivi.


01:05:23.003 --> 01:05:24.403
It's a nice option.


01:05:29.723 --> 01:05:31.124
How old are you, Toivi?


01:05:31.364 --> 01:05:32.444
I can do it.


01:05:32.644 --> 01:05:35.084
They're not cautious of me.


01:05:35.324 --> 01:05:37.364
I polish their shoes and everything.


01:05:37.604 --> 01:05:40.485
I know how to tell them
about beautiful things.


01:05:40.685 --> 01:05:42.325
They'll trust me and come.


01:05:47.085 --> 01:05:48.966
Come here, Toivi.


01:05:51.926 --> 01:05:54.326
You're going to take three officers
to the tailors,


01:06:00.527 --> 01:06:02.807
and three to the shoemakers.


01:06:03.088 --> 01:06:04.487
Arkady will take care of them.


01:06:05.407 --> 01:06:08.448
Neumann and Beckmann will stay
in the administrative corpus.


01:06:09.648 --> 01:06:10.808
Bzhetsky,


01:06:11.048 --> 01:06:12.888
you'll take two people there.


01:06:13.128 --> 01:06:15.689
I'll take care of Frenzel.
Borya, you'll cut the communication.


01:06:15.889 --> 01:06:17.729
I can't take two, I can only take one.


01:06:17.969 --> 01:06:19.729
I can bring him in and out.


01:06:21.650 --> 01:06:23.169
I have a pass.


01:06:28.530 --> 01:06:30.370
Moses, you'll go to Neumann.


01:06:33.531 --> 01:06:35.651
When we're done with the officers,


01:06:36.091 --> 01:06:39.372
Bzhetsky will give a signal for a line up.
We'll gather at the appel-platz.


01:06:42.612 --> 01:06:43.692
What is it?


01:06:44.172 --> 01:06:45.771
Did someone escape again?


01:06:48.012 --> 01:06:50.173
Don't stand close to each other in line.
You'll have a better shot at surviving.


01:06:50.413 --> 01:06:52.252
- Bzhetsky, don't sleep!
- Let's go!


01:07:50.219 --> 01:07:51.579
On your knees!


01:08:22.823 --> 01:08:25.063
Look at the puddle they've made!


01:08:25.503 --> 01:08:27.703
Smells like Jewish piss!


01:08:53.986 --> 01:08:56.826
Let's raise our glasses
to Oberscharfuhrer Frenzel!


01:08:57.066 --> 01:08:59.387
Hurray!
Music!


01:10:09.955 --> 01:10:11.915
Look, my horse is dead!


01:10:15.915 --> 01:10:18.915
You, come here!
Get moving, go!


01:10:21.236 --> 01:10:22.756
Let's go!


01:10:30.117 --> 01:10:31.236
One!


01:10:33.037 --> 01:10:34.998
Two!


01:10:38.477 --> 01:10:41.158
- Three!
- Three!


01:10:44.278 --> 01:10:45.358
Four!


01:10:47.958 --> 01:10:49.078
Five...


01:10:50.639 --> 01:10:52.199
...six...


01:10:53.080 --> 01:10:54.599
seven..


01:10:56.640 --> 01:10:57.600
...eight.


01:11:05.481 --> 01:11:07.321
You should have clean shoes


01:11:08.161 --> 01:11:11.242
when leaving for the other world.


01:11:12.201 --> 01:11:14.522
You, Jews, have no idea what beauty is.


01:11:15.082 --> 01:11:17.322
Jews don't have a sense of beauty.


01:11:18.682 --> 01:11:21.002
Dirty boots, dirty hands,


01:11:21.242 --> 01:11:22.883
dirty ears, dirty thoughts.


01:11:23.123 --> 01:11:24.602
Scum!
Dirt!


01:11:27.923 --> 01:11:30.283
Are you afraid?
Take a lesson from him!


01:11:30.523 --> 01:11:32.604
He's not afraid of anyone
or anything anymore.


01:11:35.084 --> 01:11:36.804
Polish the boots!


01:11:37.804 --> 01:11:39.044
Don't take pictures of me.


01:11:39.845 --> 01:11:41.604
I don't look so good today.


01:11:44.045 --> 01:11:46.205
Polish the boots!
Polish them!


01:11:50.366 --> 01:11:51.686
Polish the shoes!


01:11:53.926 --> 01:11:55.206
Polish them!


01:11:56.246 --> 01:11:58.127
Do it!


01:11:59.406 --> 01:12:01.287
Shit!


01:12:09.048 --> 01:12:11.367
Good job, Whipped-Ass!


01:12:11.647 --> 01:12:14.288
Let's drink together.


01:12:16.089 --> 01:12:19.369
Your faith doesn't allow you?


01:12:20.849 --> 01:12:22.729
I'll have to baptize you.


01:12:23.569 --> 01:12:26.290
Now your name is not Haim


01:12:26.850 --> 01:12:28.529
but Heinz.


01:12:29.529 --> 01:12:31.370
We're friends now, Heinz.


01:12:31.610 --> 01:12:33.010
Drink.


01:12:35.690 --> 01:12:40.170
Does your whipped ass
not appreciate the honor?


01:12:40.451 --> 01:12:42.331
Lick the floor clean.


01:12:43.691 --> 01:12:47.932
You were offered a treat by an Aryan.


01:12:48.892 --> 01:12:52.492
And you claimed you didn't drink,
your law didn't allow you to...


01:12:52.692 --> 01:12:54.572
And look at yourself lapping it up.


01:12:54.813 --> 01:12:56.813
One can never trust a Jew.


01:12:59.493 --> 01:13:02.134
I'm John the Baptist!


01:13:07.214 --> 01:13:08.614
Jews!


01:13:08.854 --> 01:13:11.374
I'm John the Baptist!


01:13:17.335 --> 01:13:20.216
John the Baptist!


01:13:21.615 --> 01:13:25.136
I am John the Baptist!


01:13:27.496 --> 01:13:29.976
Where's my wife?


01:13:30.416 --> 01:13:32.817
Give me my wife back!


01:13:33.177 --> 01:13:35.857
Give me my wife back!


01:13:36.097 --> 01:13:37.898
Here's your wife!


01:13:41.458 --> 01:13:43.778
Give me my wife back!


01:13:45.178 --> 01:13:46.578
Give me my wife back!


01:13:54.819 --> 01:13:57.019
Give me my wife back!


01:14:50.105 --> 01:14:51.505
Out of the way!


01:15:06.947 --> 01:15:08.067
Please.


01:15:11.028 --> 01:15:12.588
Should I shoot him?


01:15:14.868 --> 01:15:16.148
No.


01:15:39.030 --> 01:15:40.391
My chair.


01:15:49.152 --> 01:15:50.992
I have the fastest horse.


01:15:54.113 --> 01:15:56.072
Whoever can beat me


01:15:56.272 --> 01:15:58.553
will get a whole case of cognac!


01:16:03.713 --> 01:16:05.234
Go.


01:16:12.874 --> 01:16:14.274
Enjoy.


01:16:18.035 --> 01:16:19.275
Run.


01:16:28.676 --> 01:16:31.076
Go, go!


01:16:34.277 --> 01:16:35.637
<i>Faster!</i>


01:16:39.757 --> 01:16:40.878
<i>Faster!</i>


01:16:44.158 --> 01:16:45.718
<i>Faster!</i>


01:16:59.120 --> 01:17:00.479
<i>Run!</i>


01:17:01.960 --> 01:17:03.000
<i>Faster!</i>


01:17:19.882 --> 01:17:21.322
<i>Faster!</i>


01:17:22.802 --> 01:17:24.162
<i>Faster!</i>


01:17:26.642 --> 01:17:28.083
<i>Faster!</i>


01:17:49.325 --> 01:17:51.085
<i>Faster!</i>


01:17:53.405 --> 01:17:54.805
<i>Go!</i>


01:17:56.766 --> 01:17:58.366
<i>Faster!</i>


01:18:29.849 --> 01:18:31.209
<i>Faster!</i>


01:18:32.810 --> 01:18:35.650
Great party!
See you next time!


01:18:35.850 --> 01:18:38.411
See you!
Don't fall out of the car!


01:19:29.256 --> 01:19:30.416
Sasha!


01:19:30.616 --> 01:19:32.537
Sasha, Sasha!


01:19:33.736 --> 01:19:35.136
Sasha!


01:19:35.817 --> 01:19:39.418
Thank God!
You're alive!


01:19:39.657 --> 01:19:42.217
You're alive, Sasha...
You're alive!


01:19:42.697 --> 01:19:45.298
Sasha, Sasha!
Lord, you're alive!


01:19:46.097 --> 01:19:47.738
Sasha!


01:19:48.738 --> 01:19:50.379
Sasha!


01:19:54.579 --> 01:19:56.579
Lord, why did you do this?


01:19:59.059 --> 01:20:02.660
I just wanted to be a horse.


01:20:08.261 --> 01:20:10.020
A horse? Why?


01:20:11.260 --> 01:20:13.221
I was so scared...


01:20:13.501 --> 01:20:15.421
It was just a joke.


01:20:16.541 --> 01:20:19.222
I wanted to cheer you up.


01:20:21.741 --> 01:20:23.302
It wasn't funny!


01:20:24.382 --> 01:20:25.983
It was a bad joke!


01:20:28.262 --> 01:20:30.743
I understood what all of this is for...


01:20:31.463 --> 01:20:33.663
This war...


01:20:34.383 --> 01:20:36.383
...this damn death camp...


01:20:37.824 --> 01:20:39.303
I understood.


01:20:39.503 --> 01:20:41.904
All of this is...


01:20:46.584 --> 01:20:48.185
...is what?


01:20:49.505 --> 01:20:51.425
...to find you.


01:21:36.790 --> 01:21:39.150
I feel so good now...


01:21:40.710 --> 01:21:41.831
Really?


01:21:47.351 --> 01:21:48.632
Lord...


01:21:50.431 --> 01:21:51.832
Thank you.


01:22:37.516 --> 01:22:38.717
Look carefully.


01:22:38.957 --> 01:22:40.557
Take the stool,


01:22:40.797 --> 01:22:42.358
put it right here,


01:22:42.598 --> 01:22:44.477
so that when the German sits down,


01:22:44.677 --> 01:22:46.918
he'll have his back to Arkady.


01:22:48.318 --> 01:22:49.318
Got it?


01:22:50.198 --> 01:22:51.598
I understand.


01:22:53.999 --> 01:22:55.918
I'll show you again just in case.


01:22:57.279 --> 01:23:00.559
Take the stool, put it right here,


01:23:01.519 --> 01:23:04.320
so that the German's back
is facing Arkady.


01:23:04.520 --> 01:23:05.640
Clear?


01:23:05.880 --> 01:23:07.480
I understand, yes.


01:23:09.440 --> 01:23:11.161
Alright, show me, then.


01:23:17.601 --> 01:23:18.681
Like this?


01:23:19.721 --> 01:23:20.881
Yes.


01:23:23.482 --> 01:23:24.721
And you, Arkady...


01:23:26.002 --> 01:23:27.722
Go, Borya, go!


01:23:28.643 --> 01:23:30.602
Well, if you know everything...


01:23:33.523 --> 01:23:37.003
It's a great coat, a very fashionable one.


01:23:37.243 --> 01:23:39.924
Well, if you don't want it,
I'll go to Beckmann.


01:23:40.164 --> 01:23:42.563
Beckmann can do without it.
Let's go.


01:23:43.924 --> 01:23:47.085
If the coat is really good,
I'll give you some sugar.


01:23:47.884 --> 01:23:49.844
You like sugar, don't you?


01:23:50.645 --> 01:23:53.485
Yes, very much, Mr. Berg!


01:24:02.406 --> 01:24:03.726
They're coming!


01:24:13.247 --> 01:24:15.128
You're early!
I am not done yet!


01:24:15.328 --> 01:24:17.607
Unterscharfuhrer could only come now.


01:24:18.007 --> 01:24:19.848
Come to the light.


01:24:20.448 --> 01:24:22.689
Yes, yes!


01:24:26.289 --> 01:24:28.449
Wagner and Beckmann will burst with envy.


01:25:15.254 --> 01:25:16.574
Here.


01:25:21.895 --> 01:25:23.375
Come here.


01:25:43.137 --> 01:25:44.578
Jew!


01:25:46.777 --> 01:25:48.698
Give me the weapon!


01:25:48.898 --> 01:25:50.418
It's not for you!


01:25:54.498 --> 01:25:56.259
You won't dare to shoot!


01:25:57.379 --> 01:25:59.339
It'll cause too much noise.


01:26:04.779 --> 01:26:06.580
Too much noise?


01:26:06.820 --> 01:26:08.580
Well, I'll do it noiselessly then.


01:26:36.863 --> 01:26:38.544
Why did you go quiet?


01:26:38.744 --> 01:26:40.543
Work, work!


01:26:42.904 --> 01:26:44.384
Work!


01:26:47.864 --> 01:26:50.105
Just for you, Mr. Unterscharfuhrer,


01:26:50.345 --> 01:26:52.184
specially for you, a leather cloak.


01:26:53.025 --> 01:26:54.425
Only for you!


01:26:54.625 --> 01:26:56.466
An expensive piece from Paris!


01:27:00.906 --> 01:27:03.185
He knelt in front of me, this scum.


01:27:04.106 --> 01:27:05.706
He's got no pride.


01:27:11.187 --> 01:27:12.547
You did well, Yusef.


01:27:13.507 --> 01:27:14.987
Yes, I did well...


01:27:15.787 --> 01:27:18.068
I had a wife and four kids.


01:27:18.508 --> 01:27:19.628
I did well...


01:27:20.867 --> 01:27:22.908
Something just for you,
Mr. Oberscharfuhrer!


01:27:23.388 --> 01:27:24.708
Come!


01:27:33.949 --> 01:27:36.350
An expensive item,
straight from Paris.


01:27:43.831 --> 01:27:44.990
<i>Where?</i>


01:27:46.070 --> 01:27:47.311
I'm sorry...


01:27:47.511 --> 01:27:49.951
This is specially for you,
Mr. Oberscharfuhrer.


01:27:50.191 --> 01:27:53.512
A leather coat.
A priceless piece, from Paris.


01:27:56.511 --> 01:27:59.312
Does Beckmann have anything like this?


01:28:01.313 --> 01:28:03.592
It's one-of-a-kind!
What do you think?


01:28:04.593 --> 01:28:08.233
Beckmann has a fetish
for fine leather goods.


01:28:09.713 --> 01:28:12.074
Should I offer it to Mr. Beckmann then?


01:28:13.074 --> 01:28:15.914
Why would you?
I'm taking this coat with me.


01:28:17.794 --> 01:28:18.915
<i>Try it on..</i>


01:28:20.074 --> 01:28:22.235
I'll make alterations...


01:28:24.355 --> 01:28:26.515
...so that it fits you perfectly.


01:28:28.675 --> 01:28:30.436
Everyone will admire you!


01:28:33.356 --> 01:28:34.596
Well, okay.


01:28:38.716 --> 01:28:40.077
But make it quick.


01:28:50.998 --> 01:28:52.318
A Photo?


01:28:52.558 --> 01:28:53.558
Sure.


01:29:28.522 --> 01:29:31.002
Where are those boots
I've been hearing about?


01:29:31.442 --> 01:29:33.242
Please, try them on.


01:29:53.125 --> 01:29:55.124
Don't piss yourself, little Jew...


01:30:19.047 --> 01:30:20.608
I'll kill you myself.


01:30:21.328 --> 01:30:23.847
Women tell me I smell like a corpse.


01:30:25.168 --> 01:30:27.128
I am Death!


01:30:52.931 --> 01:30:55.811
Boy, where are you?


01:30:58.292 --> 01:31:00.132
I'll punish you!


01:31:01.332 --> 01:31:03.653
Mommy...
Mommy...


01:31:13.093 --> 01:31:14.334
What are you doing here?


01:31:14.574 --> 01:31:15.974
I've brought you a pin.


01:31:16.214 --> 01:31:17.574
Put it down.


01:32:27.621 --> 01:32:29.582
Did you want cuff links?


01:32:34.182 --> 01:32:36.463
I'll make them out of your teeth!


01:33:01.305 --> 01:33:03.185
You taught the Jews to kill...


01:33:19.748 --> 01:33:21.467
You're just in time!


01:33:26.948 --> 01:33:30.269
You'll take a knife and then go
and stab him.


01:33:30.469 --> 01:33:32.988
Kill me... kill me...


01:33:33.228 --> 01:33:35.029
- I can't...
- Don't be afraid of him.


01:33:35.229 --> 01:33:36.989
- I'm sorry...
- You should be afraid of me!


01:33:37.229 --> 01:33:38.869
Leave him alone!


01:33:40.189 --> 01:33:41.630
- It's ready, commander.
- Good job.


01:33:41.870 --> 01:33:43.350
Sasha, Moses can't do it.
He's afraid of blood.


01:33:43.550 --> 01:33:45.430
- Who will go to Neumann?
- Where's Bzhetsky?


01:33:45.670 --> 01:33:47.310
- Go to Bzhetsky fast!
- Okay!


01:33:47.550 --> 01:33:49.231
Leo, I've got it.


01:33:50.190 --> 01:33:52.191
You're so brave, my girl.


01:34:01.272 --> 01:34:03.192
I've killed Neumann.


01:34:07.753 --> 01:34:09.953
Good job, boy, good job!


01:34:11.153 --> 01:34:12.993
Sasha, there are so many bullets there!


01:34:13.234 --> 01:34:15.393
Sasha, it's enough for us to break free.
Let's do it now!


01:34:15.633 --> 01:34:17.754
No, Borya, no.
The whole camp will escape.


01:34:23.634 --> 01:34:25.514
I've killed a human.


01:34:30.996 --> 01:34:32.515
I've killed him.


01:34:34.115 --> 01:34:36.436
Leo, which one of your people
can get to Beckmann now?


01:34:36.676 --> 01:34:38.516
- I don't know.
- I can!


01:34:43.956 --> 01:34:45.877
I have access to that barrack.


01:34:46.677 --> 01:34:48.677
Selma, tell them I can do it.


01:35:15.640 --> 01:35:18.081
Would you like some hot water with sugar?


01:35:26.321 --> 01:35:28.081
No!


01:35:29.722 --> 01:35:31.882
I'll never eat sugar again.


01:35:37.682 --> 01:35:39.683
They've taken your childhood
away from you.


01:35:43.963 --> 01:35:47.004
And you're helping us
to take their lives away.


01:35:47.204 --> 01:35:48.523
It's fair, Toivi.


01:35:54.964 --> 01:35:56.324
Find Shlomo


01:35:56.564 --> 01:35:59.085
and don't take your eyes off Frenzel.


01:36:01.085 --> 01:36:02.645
He'll handle it, Sasha.


01:36:25.327 --> 01:36:27.248
How could you do it?


01:36:27.488 --> 01:36:31.088
What do you have in your heart
that they've listened to you?


01:36:32.448 --> 01:36:34.769
Sasha has Stalin in his heart.


01:36:36.008 --> 01:36:37.529
Just like all of us.


01:38:47.263 --> 01:38:48.864
Where is everyone?


01:38:55.144 --> 01:38:56.665
What's going on?


01:38:56.865 --> 01:38:58.224
Where is everyone?


01:39:34.348 --> 01:39:36.069
Get the people up!


01:39:36.309 --> 01:39:37.749
Get them up!


01:39:37.949 --> 01:39:39.789
Get up! Everyone,get up!


01:39:47.150 --> 01:39:48.830
Leo!


01:39:49.030 --> 01:39:50.430
Tell them to run!


01:39:50.670 --> 01:39:52.230
Tell them to run!


01:39:52.470 --> 01:39:54.071
Run, run!


01:39:54.791 --> 01:39:56.871
Get up!
Get up!


01:40:11.913 --> 01:40:14.753
Run!
Run!


01:41:05.879 --> 01:41:07.518
Come on!


01:41:09.479 --> 01:41:10.759
Come on!


01:41:21.200 --> 01:41:22.440
Come on!


01:41:24.161 --> 01:41:25.760
Let's go!


01:41:36.921 --> 01:41:38.802
It'll be alright!


01:41:39.802 --> 01:41:42.962
Please, please, Silent!


01:41:43.202 --> 01:41:45.523
Let's go!


01:41:45.763 --> 01:41:47.603
I beg you, let's go!


01:42:17.567 --> 01:42:19.086
You've jinxed it.


01:42:40.609 --> 01:42:42.049
Lyuka!


01:42:42.249 --> 01:42:43.449
Lyuka!


01:42:44.129 --> 01:42:45.370
Lyuka!


01:42:46.450 --> 01:42:49.810
Lyuka, Lyuka!


01:42:50.490 --> 01:42:53.530
Sasha, Sasha, Sasha!

